        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "This is with explicit backticks. Although I like the look a lot, it might have one small disadvantage: you can't search for a function using `/^nvim_` anymore, but need (to know) to use ``/^`nvim_``\n\n<details><summary>Function definitions in :help</summary>\n<p>\n<img width=\"670\" height=\"481\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/aae079dd-96ee-4f3d-a387-61f7a29bb628\" />\n</p>\n</details> \n\n\n\n<details><summary>Function definitions on neovim.io</summary>\n<p>\n<img width=\"826\" height=\"733\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/2a8abae9-7ad5-4943-b24d-6ec87e84900b\" />\n</p>\n</details> \n\n\n",
